acy computer codes. Technometrics, 55(1):37–46, 2013. [27] Julien Villemonteix, Emmanuel Vazquez, and Eric Walter. An informational approach to the global optimization of expensive-to-evaluate functions. Journal of Global Optimization, 44(4): 509–534, 2009. [28] Julien Bect, David Ginsbourger, Ling Li, Victor Picheny, and Emmanuel Vazquez. Sequential design of computer experiments for the estimation of a probability of failure. Statistics and Computing, 22(3):773–793, 2012. [29] Jialin Song, Yuxin Chen, and Yisong Yue. A general framework for multi-fidelity bayesian optimization with gaussian processes. In The 22nd International Conference on Artificial In- telligence and Statistics, pages 3158–3167. PMLR, 2019. [30] Jian Wu, Saul Toscano-Palmerin, Peter I Frazier, and Andrew Gordon Wilson. Practical multi- fidelity bayesian optimization for hyperparameter tuning. In Uncertainty in Artificial Intelli- gence, pages 788–798. PMLR, 2020. [31] Kirthevasan Kandasamy, Gautam Dasarathy, Jeff Schneider, and Barnab´as P´oczos. Multi- fidelity bayesian optimisation with continuous approximations. In International Conference on Machine Learning, pages 1799–1808. PMLR, 2017. [32] Xu He, Rui Tuo, and CF Jeff Wu. Optimization of multi-fidelity computer experiments via the eqie criterion. Technometrics, 59(1):58–68, 2017. [33] Tor Lattimore and Csaba Szepesv´ari. Bandit algorithms. Cambridge University Press, 2020. [34] Tze Leung Lai, Herbert Robbins, et al. Asymptotically efficient adaptive allocation rules. Advances in applied mathematics, 6(1):4–22, 1985. [35] Andreas Krause and Daniel Golovin. Submodular function maximization. Tractability, 3: 71–104, 2014. 6 [36] Peter Fretwell, Hamish D Pritchard, David G Vaughan, Jonathan L Bamber, Nicholas E Bar- rand, R Bell, C Bianchi, RG Bingham, Donald D Blankenship, G Casassa, et al. Bedmap2: improved ice bed, surface and thickness datasets for antarctica. The Cryosphere, 7(1):375–393, 2013. [37] Romain Millan, Eric J Rignot, Mathieu 